course: dictionary
lesson: 11040
title: Weary: tired, or fed up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Weary has a few meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. The most common is very tired, often after hard work or a long journey. «Where weary harvesters could line up in scores along the table» means the farm workers were worn out after their work and ready to eat.
explain: The second meaning is bored or fed up with something because there has been too much of it. You can be weary of the rain or weary of waiting. Weary can also be a verb: «The long walk wearied us» means the walk made us tired.
explain: To check your meaning, swap a word into the sentence. Try tired in «the weary harvesters». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Then look at the clues around the word to see which sense fits best.
fact: Weary means very tired, especially after a lot of work or a long journey.
fact: Weary of something means fed up with it after too much of it, as in «weary of the rain».
fact: To weary means to make or become tired: «The long walk wearied us.»
fact: Weary can be an adjective (weary, wearier, weariest) or a verb (weary, wearies, wearied, wearying).
fact: In the Bible, Jesus says, «Come to me, all you who are weary», and he offers rest.
exercise: «The harvesters were weary after a long day in the fields.» What does weary mean here? | *Very tired | Fast and lively | Very happy | Wide awake and full of energy
exercise: Ana says, «I am weary of the rain.» What does weary of mean? | Happy to splash in puddles | *Fed up with it after too much of it | Full of joy at the rain | Afraid of the rain
exercise: In «The long walk wearied us», what kind of word is wearied? | *A verb, a word for an action that means to make tired | An adverb, a word for how something is done | A noun, a name for a thing | An adjective, a word for describing
test: The book says «where weary harvesters could line up». Which word in the sentence tells you the harvesters are tired after work? | table | line | harvesters | *weary
test: Dad says, «I am weary of the noise.» What does he mean? | *He is fed up with the noise | He is very happy with the noise | He cannot hear the noise | He is making the noise
exam: Which word means fed up after too much of something? | *Weary | Luminous | Curt | Famished
